Third-party data included in this repository
--------------------------------------------

tests/fixtures/advisories/ contains unmodified security advisories from the
GitHub Advisory Database (https://github.com/github/advisory-database),
licensed under CC-BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
Text from those advisories also appears in the example reports under
examples/.

tests/fixtures/advisories/npm/MAL-2026-900001.json is not a real advisory.
It was written for cvescan's own tests, as were the "known exploited" (KEV),
EPSS and end-of-life data generated by tests/fixtures/make_upstream.py.


Software downloaded at build time, not included in this repository
------------------------------------------------------------------

The container image built by install.sh contains osv-scanner
(https://github.com/google/osv-scanner), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. The build downloads a release binary and checks it against a
pinned SHA-256.
